{"rue":{"id":"820919db-92b1-4626-87f0-c4c52dbbd5ac","word":"rue","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"any of various perennial shrubs of the genus Ruta","tags":["feminine"],"word":"arruda"}],"pos":"noun","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"But th'aged Nourse, her calling to her bowre, / Had gathered Rew, and Savine, and the flowre / Of Camphora, and Calamint, and Dill [...].","ref":"1590, Edmund Spenser, “Book III, Canto II”, in The Faerie Queene. […], London: […] [John Wolfe] for William Ponsonbie, →OCLC:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[61,64]],"id":"fae217bf-ac63-4cc1-bff5-a77bc1bd9b39"},{"text":"Ophelia:\nThere’s fennel for you, and columbines: there’s rue for you; and here’s some for me: we may call it herb-grace o' Sundays: O you must wear your rue with a difference.","ref":"c. 1599–1602 (date written), William Shakespeare, “The Tragedie of Hamlet, Prince of Denmarke”, in Mr. William Shakespeares Comedies, Histories, & Tragedies […] (First Folio), London: […] Isaac Iaggard, and Ed[ward] Blount, published 1623, →OCLC, [Act IV, scene v]:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[57,60],[153,156]],"id":"64799737-af00-415a-beb5-8c2a68d59163"},{"text":"The life of one plant would be affected by another. Rue was definitely hostile to basil, rosemary to hyssop, but coriander, dill and chervil lived on the friendliest of terms[.]","ref":"1940, Rosetta E. Clarkson, Green Enchantments: The Magic Spell of Gardens, The Macmillan Company, page 253:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[52,55]],"id":"2e3d41bb-8077-494b-b0bc-bcfbed48f022"},{"text":"Like the water lily, endive, and lettuce, rue was believed to have anti-aphrodisiac properties.","ref":"1961, Harry E. Wedeck, Dictionary of Aphrodisiacs, New York: The Citadel Press, page 211:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[42,45]],"id":"5a479412-f32e-4c5c-ae79-f07dcbc055c6"}],"senseid":["en:plant"],"links":[["perennial","perennial"],["shrubs","shrubs"],["Ruta","Ruta"],["Ruta graveolens","Ruta graveolens#Translingual"],["common rue","common rue"]],"categories":["English terms with quotations"],"glosses":["Any of various perennial shrubs of the genus Ruta, especially the herb Ruta graveolens (common rue), formerly used in medicines."],"tags":["countable","uncountable"],"id":"a04274c3-736c-44a5-87b6-31074046c217"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[]},"rueful":{"id":"d4978931-3f51-4e41-9c96-81bdc715bb56","word":"rueful","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"causing, feeling, or expressing regret or sorrow","word":"recalcado"}],"pos":"adj","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"Merely, he received it with the rueful indulgence that he would show towards Tom when he came through with one of his solutions for ending world poverty or the arms race.","ref":"1986, John le Carré, A Perfect Spy:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[32,38]],"id":"19c048ca-c4b6-4182-ac16-6dcb16e08e56"}],"links":[["regret","regret"],["sorrow","sorrow"],["wry","wry"]],"synonyms":[{"word":"deplorable"},{"word":"pitiful"},{"word":"sorry"},{"word":"atrabiliary","source":"Thesaurus:lamentable"},{"word":"atrabilious","source":"Thesaurus:lamentable"},{"word":"deplorable","source":"Thesaurus:lamentable"},{"word":"depressing","source":"Thesaurus:lamentable"},{"word":"distressing","source":"Thesaurus:lamentable"},{"word":"grievous","source":"Thesaurus:lamentable"},{"word":"heartbreaking","source":"Thesaurus:lamentable"},{"word":"heartrending","source":"Thesaurus:lamentable"},{"word":"miserable","source":"Thesaurus:lamentable","tags":["obsolete"]},{"word":"lamentable","source":"Thesaurus:lamentable"},{"word":"lachrymable","source":"Thesaurus:lamentable","tags":["archaic"]},{"word":"mournful","source":"Thesaurus:lamentable"},{"word":"regrettable","source":"Thesaurus:lamentable"},{"word":"rueful","source":"Thesaurus:lamentable"},{"word":"sad","source":"Thesaurus:lamentable"},{"word":"saddening","source":"Thesaurus:lamentable"},{"word":"sorr